As show in~\cite[\S 5.2.1]{leiloefflerzerbes10}, we have $H^1_{\mathrm{Iw}}(\mathbb Q_p,T)^i=H^1_{\mathrm{Iw}}(\mathbb Q_p,T)\cap\ker(\underline{\mathrm{Col}}_i)$ for the Coleman maps
   \[ \underline{\mathrm{Col}}_i: H^1_{\mathrm{Iw}}(\mathbb Q_p,T)\rTo\Lambda(\Gamma)\]
   defined in {\em op.cit.}

In \cite{leiloefflerzerbes10}, we have defined two pairs of Coleman maps (with respect to the chosen basis),  
    \begin{align*}
     \mathrm{Col}_i:\mathbb N(V)^{\psi=1} & \rTo(\mathbb B_{\mathbb Q_p}^+)^{\psi=0}, \hspace{3ex}\text{and} \\
     \underline{\mathrm{Col}}_i:\mathbb N(V)^{\psi=1} & \rTo\Lambda_{\mathbb Q_p}(\Gamma)
    \end{align*}
    for $i=1,2$ with the following properties: for $x\in\mathbb N(V)^{\psi=1}$, write $x=(x_1\bar{n}_1+x_2\bar{n}_2)\otimes \pi^{-1}e_1$ where $x_1,x_2\in\mathbb B_{\mathbb Q_p}^+$. Then
    \begin{align} (1-\varphi)(x) & =\begin{pmatrix}\mathrm{Col}_1(x) & \mathrm{Col}_2(x) \end{pmatrix}M\begin{pmatrix}\bar{\nu}_1\\\bar{\nu}_2\end{pmatrix}\otimes t^{-1}e_1 \\
     & =\begin{pmatrix}\underline{\mathrm{Col}}_1(x) & \underline{\mathrm{Col}}_2(x) \end{pmatrix}\cdot[(1+\pi)M]\begin{pmatrix}\bar{\nu}_1\\\bar{\nu}_2\end{pmatrix}\otimes t^{-1}e_1
    \end{align}
    where  $M=\frac{t}{\pi q}P^T(M')^{-1}$.

